  "behavior": [
    "TableView and TableGrid configure scalar settings, nullable IDs and titles through native owned columns.",
    "Native column snapshots preserve resolved values and geometry. Language text owns an independent result across replacement and destruction.",
    "Both output failure prefixes preserve all previous tuple assignments and balance XRT live allocations.",
    "One thousand warmed getters for null ID/title allocate nothing, as do direct C borrowed getters. Two nonempty text fields add two balanced XRT allocations per language getter.",
    "Legacy header sorting, table event dispatch and grid editing pass their functional control. The legacy fixtures finish with the same 1 live XRT allocation of 764 requested bytes on the preceding and current SDKs.",
    "Each expanded native column is 128 bytes on the tested x64 configurations. Array projection and a 64-entry native stack staging area are cold setting costs."
  ],
